## Architecture Diagram

```
backup.conf                          .backup-state.json
    │                                        │
    ▼                                        ▼
┌──────────────────┐              ┌─────────────────────┐
│ BackupConfigParser│              │   Persisted State    │
│                  │              │  ┌───────────────┐  │
│  [general]       │              │  │ Snapshot #1    │  │
│  [schedule]      │──► BackupConfig │  (full)        │  │
│  [incremental]   │       │      │  ├───────────────┤  │
│  [include]       │       │      │  │ Snapshot #2    │  │
│  [exclude]       │       │      │  │  (incremental) │  │
└──────────────────┘       │      │  ├───────────────┤  │
                           ▼      │  │ Snapshot #3    │  │
                ┌──────────────┐  │  │  (incremental) │  │
                │  Incremental │  │  └───────────────┘  │
                │ BackupEngine │◄─┘                     │
                │              │──────────────────────►  │
                │  • scan()    │    save updated state   │
                │  • diff()    │                         │
                │  • retain()  │  ┌───────────────────┐  │
                └──────┬───────┘  │  Diff Report       │  │
                       │          │  + added: 3        │  │
                       └─────────►│  + modified: 1     │  │
                                  │  + deleted: 2      │  │
                                  │  + unchanged: 44   │  │
                                  └───────────────────┘

Incremental Cycle Logic:
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Cycle 1  →  FULL        (no prior state)
  Cycle 2  →  incremental (diff vs snapshot 1)
  Cycle 3  →  incremental (diff vs snapshot 2)
  Cycle 4  →  FULL        (full_backup_interval=3)
  Cycle 5  →  incremental (diff vs snapshot 4)
  ...
```

## Key Design Points

| Concept | How It Works |
|---|---|
| **Config parsing** | INI-style parser handles sections, typed values, arrays (`key[]`), inline comments |
| **Validation** | Schema-driven — required fields, type checking, allowed values, range checks |
| **Snapshots** | Each backup run creates a `Snapshot` containing `FileEntry` metadata for every file |
| **Change detection** | SHA-256 checksums + size + mtime comparison between current and previous snapshot |
| **Full vs incremental** | Full backup runs every N cycles (configurable) or when no prior state exists |
| **Retention** | Old snapshots pruned by age (`retention_days`) and count (`max_full_backups`) |
| **Exclusion** | Glob-like pattern matching for `*.ext`, `dirname/`, and exact filenames |
| **Events** | Engine extends `EventEmitter` for logging/monitoring hooks |

